ums512_1h10: drop the unused cp_boot.h include from extlinux_diag.c

cp_boot.h defines three functions with external linkage in the header
itself - get_sp_bootcode_size(), get_sp_bootcode_buf() (under
CONFIG_SP_DDR_BOOT) and pmic_arm7_RAM_active() (under
CONFIG_ARM7_RAM_ACTIVE). That only works while exactly one translation
unit includes it, which was the case: modem_entry.c is the definition
site, and loader_nvm.c, sysdump.c and process_cp_coupling_info.c call
them through extern declarations.

extlinux_diag.c became a second includer, so both objects define the
same three symbols and the board link fails:

  board/spreadtrum/ums512_1h10/cp_boot.h:92: multiple definition of
      'get_sp_bootcode_size'; modem_entry.o: first defined here

extlinux_diag.c does not use anything from cp_boot.h - not one of its
symbols is referenced - and the header has no includes of its own, so
there is nothing to inherit from it either. The register definitions it
does need (aon_apb.h, pmu_apb.h) are already included directly.

Drop the include. Making the three functions static inline instead would
break the extern callers listed above, and moving them into a .c file is
a larger change to vendor code for no gain here.

Signed-off-by: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>

diff --git a/board/spreadtrum/ums512_1h10/extlinux_diag.c b/board/spreadtrum/ums512_1h10/extlinux_diag.c
index 5eab53c..ce7abd1 100644
--- a/board/spreadtrum/ums512_1h10/extlinux_diag.c
+++ b/board/spreadtrum/ums512_1h10/extlinux_diag.c
@@ -18,7 +18,6 @@
 
 #include <asm/arch-sharkl5pro/chip_sharkl5pro/aon_apb.h>
 #include <asm/arch-sharkl5pro/chip_sharkl5pro/pmu_apb.h>
-#include "cp_boot.h"
 
 /* Charge screen tuning. */
 #define CHARGE_SPLASH_MS	3000	/* how long the "Charging..." text stays lit */
